  "latest_nl_proof": "Let x be an arbitrary real number, and set m = floor(x). By the defining property of the floor function, m is an integer such that m <= x < m + 1. Subtracting m from the inequality x < m + 1 gives x - m < 1. Since m = floor(x), this is exactly x - floor(x) < 1. Because x was arbitrary, the inequality holds for every real number x.",
